# .trivyignore
#
# One finding per line, each with a comment saying WHY it is accepted and who
# accepted it. An entry without a reason is indistinguishable from an entry
# nobody can justify, and that is how an ignore file becomes the place problems
# go to be forgotten.
#
# Nothing belongs here merely because upstream has not patched it. `scan`
# passes --ignore-unfixed, which already drops unfixed CVEs; this file is only
# for findings that ARE fixable and that we are choosing to carry anyway.
#
# Format:
#   CVE-2026-12345  # <why accepted> - <date> - <who>
#
# Empty on purpose.
